# Tag control 0: the message goes as the host sent it. A tagged join keeps its
# VID, and one that is on a row's VLAN is held to that row; an untagged join
# says nothing of a VLAN (an extended VLAN rule may tag it on the way), so the
# ranges alone decide.
0 policy
snooping=1
igmp_function=0
immediate_leave=1
allow=225.1.0.0-225.1.255.255 v=100
allow=225.2.0.0-225.2.255.255 v=200
end
0 tick
1 v2join 1 100 192.168.1.10 225.1.1.1
2 v2join 1 100 192.168.1.10 225.2.1.1
3 v2join 1 200 192.168.1.10 225.2.1.1
4 v2join 1 0 192.168.1.10 225.2.1.2
5 state
